+Keep one authoritative board per event. Editors submit commands over HTTPS; browsers display a revisioned view of the board. Committed changes reach browsers over self-hosted WebSocket sessions: the server holds each browser's connection and pushes committed revisions as they land. Self-hosting gives fast updates without a recurring realtime vendor bill or provider coupling. It accepts connection-capacity, reconnect, and reliable-publication work that a hosted service would absorb.
 
