+Delivery, change storage, and browser recovery are designed together around the socket approach. The change store retains replayable revisions so a reconnecting browser can catch up from its last-seen revision, and it publishes committed revisions reliably to the delivery layer. Delivery manages socket sessions and connection capacity. Browser sync subscribes, reconnects, and catches up from the last revision it received.
 
